                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "a5596bd7-5611-4211-aef7-d6eae7031366",
                                "sense_id": "cf14fb6b-06af-3c94-8d07-e0c7dec8e235",
                                "text": "Des animations autour de la neurodiversité seront également proposées."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "f9821d5d-5699-30cb-8174-2777bad76c20",
                        "entry_id": "33075006-39dc-3d00-b4f1-166b5648a280",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Mouvements sociaux visant à faire reconnaître et accepter cette différence."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "cdd71213-c636-4c2c-8c61-b675cedc0445",
                                "sense_id": "f9821d5d-5699-30cb-8174-2777bad76c20",
                                "text": "La notion de neurodiversité existe depuis plusieurs années sans être nommée ainsi. L’initiation du mot « neurodiversité » est attribué à une autiste militante, Judy Singer, dans les années 1998-1999. Le journaliste Harvey Blume a utilisé ce terme publiquement en 1998."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "40d74fa0-1ee7-4225-a4fd-b393ce8c701f",
                        "source_entry_id": "33075006-39dc-3d00-b4f1-166b5648a280",
                        "target_lang_word": "Neurodiversität",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": []
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "0f9bc3bd-020e-4294-bdbc-1feeca8629ba",
                        "source_entry_id": "33075006-39dc-3d00-b4f1-166b5648a280",
                        "target_lang_word": "neurodiversity",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "neurodiversity",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bff7d679-94aa-34cd-b6a0-7e545cbb0e5c",
                                        "entry_id": "0432b0c0-819d-3963-b98f-079ace7e336f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The variety of configurations of the brain, especially with regard to autism."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7e7f770f-005b-437a-8873-95c10a341208",
                                                "sense_id": "bff7d679-94aa-34cd-b6a0-7e545cbb0e5c",
                                                "text": "For me, the significance of the \"Autistic Spectrum\" lies in its call for and anticipation of a \"Politics of Neurodiversity\". […] The rise of Neurodiversity takes postmodern fragmentation one step further."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2fadd8b5-e383-4f9e-83ca-6da73efc644d",
                                                "sense_id": "bff7d679-94aa-34cd-b6a0-7e545cbb0e5c",
                                                "text": "Neurodiversity may be every bit as crucial for the human race as biodiversity is for life in general. Who can say what form of wiring will prove best at any given moment? Cybernetics and computer culture, for example, may favor a somewhat autistic cast of mind."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3a03f98d-ef0d-4cfa-b518-bd8e80d307a3",
                                                "sense_id": "bff7d679-94aa-34cd-b6a0-7e545cbb0e5c",
                                                "text": "The Neurodiversity movement is progressing towards an acceptance in mainstream business. Neurodiversity inclusion is increasingly likely to be present in EDI [equality, diversity, and inclusion] policies alongside gender, race and LGBTQIA+ in many leading industries (though I note that disability more broadly is lagging behind)."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
